  source_lineage: building-trust.md
  notes: >-
    A Kenya-based network letting people exchange Community Asset Vouchers
    (promises of future goods/labor/services) through shared "commitment
    pools" that track who has offered, taken, and fulfilled promises over
    time. Cited in the article as the clearest working example of trust
    backed by relationships rather than substituted by technology.
